        {
          "position": 1,
          "kind": "comparison",
          "text": "Ta. veyil ‘sun-light’, veyil-ōn ‘sun’; Te. vēvelugu ‘sun’; old. Ka. bisil ‘sunlight’; Kui vēla ‘sun’, Poya vēl ‘id.’"
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "kind": "source-commentary",
          "text": "Some Kolarian languages like Kharia, Juang, Gadba, etc. have words like beru, bero, bel, ber, bela, etc. for ‘sun’. But that word-group seems to have a different source"
        }
      ],
      "comparison_endpoint_status": "unresolved; no graph edges emitted",
      "relationship_review": "The author distinguishes the Kolarian sun word group as apparently having a different source. Do not infer cognacy from this passage or assign its unpaired forms to individual languages."
